! REPRODUCER, an ASSEMBLER finding (docs/NEXT.md, "G2.1 CHAPTER 4: WHAT
! THE ASSEMBLER REFUSES IN A DD(N)").  strap_asm.py refuses this deck:
!
!   DD(N) literal '0X11' is zero, which is not implemented (no listed
!   example)
!
! THERE IS A PRINTED EXAMPLE NOW, though not a listed one.  C22-6578
! printed p.46 (Problem 4.11) has "E11 DD(N), 0X11" and uses it as the
! operand of "D+(U), E11" to force the accumulator's exponent to 11, so
! the word must be a ZERO FRACTION WITH EXPONENT +11: X "overrules and
! replaces the exponent computed by STRAP" (C28-6129 printed p.27).
! That is 0160 0000 0000 0000 (Reference Manual printed p.78: exponent
! magnitude in bits 1-10).  The same book has "DD(N), 0.0" (printed
! p.49, the lower limit of Problem 4.13's integral, and LEGQ8Z p.50)
! and "DD(N), 0" (ZERO, Problem 4.8 printed p.42).
!
! WHAT A ZERO WITHOUT AN X COMPILES TO IS NOT SETTLED BY THESE PAGES.
! The program at p.49 only needs 0.0 to be a zero fraction; exponent 0
! and the machine's own "normal order of magnitude zero" would both
! run.  No listing in the corpus prints one.
! tests/check_problem_4_dd_refusals.py asserts the refusal.

START   BEW, $
E11     DD(N), 0X11
        END, START
